<!--
    Integration_Event__e — Custom Platform Event
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    Platform Events are Salesforce's event-driven messaging backbone.
    They implement the publish-subscribe (pub/sub) pattern.

    PUBLISH BEHAVIOR OPTIONS:
    ══════════════════════════
    PublishAfterCommit (recommended):
      • Events are published ONLY when the publishing transaction commits
      • If the transaction rolls back (exception, DML error), NO event is sent
      • Guarantees consistency: subscribers always see committed data
      • Slightly higher latency (waits for commit)

    PublishImmediately:
      • Events are published as soon as EventBus.publish() is called
      • Even if the publishing transaction rolls back, the event IS sent
      • Use for audit/logging where you want to capture all attempts
      • Lower latency; not tied to transaction outcome

    EVENT TYPE OPTIONS:
    ═══════════════════
    StandardVolume (this object):
      • Events retained for 72 hours (replay window)
      • Max 250,000 events/hour across all Standard Volume events
      • Subscribers can replay from any point within 72 hours using ReplayId
      • Accessible via CometD, Apex triggers, Flows, LWC, External systems

    HighVolume:
      • No retention / replay (events not stored)
      • Higher throughput (up to 500,000 events/hour)
      • Accessible via Pub/Sub API (gRPC) only — not CometD
      • Use for telemetry, IoT, high-frequency integrations

    GOVERNOR LIMITS:
    ════════════════
    • Max 2,000 publish calls per transaction (single or bulk)
    • Max 500,000 StandardVolume events published per hour per org
    • Max 250,000 Platform Event trigger invocations per hour
    • Events delivered to subscribers within seconds of commit
-->
<CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <deploymentStatus>Deployed</deploymentStatus>
    <description>General-purpose integration event for demonstrating Platform Events pub/sub patterns. Published after transaction commit to guarantee data consistency.</description>
    <eventType>StandardVolume</eventType>
    <label>Integration Event</label>
    <pluralLabel>Integration Events</pluralLabel>
    <publishBehavior>PublishAfterCommit</publishBehavior>
</CustomObject>
